\begin{aligned}
t &= \frac{-26 \pm \sqrt{26^2 - 4(-16)(105)}}{2(-16)} \\
&= \frac{-26 \pm \sqrt{676 + 6720}}{-32} \\
&= \frac{-26 \pm \sqrt{7396}}{-32} \\
&= \frac{-26 \pm 86}{-32}
\end{aligned}
\]

The two solutions are $t = \frac{-26 + 86}{-32} = \frac{60}{-32} = -1.875$ and $t = \frac{-26 - 86}{-32} = \frac{-112}{-32} = 3.5$. However, time cannot be negative, so we discard the negative solution. Thus, $t \approx 3.6$.</think> <answer> 3.6</answer>

